{
  "_comment": "THE CONVERSATIONAL LOOP - PLAN 2x §3.3. The AI writes this file and bumps `rev`; the Texture panel polls /api/textureparams once a second and regenerates on a rev change. `autoplay` is absent BY DESIGN - sound only ever on the composer SPACE or Play. Every label must NAME THE DIALS IT MOVED (§6 two-sided contract).",
  "_slate": "rev 4 (2026-08-20, day 21) - THE ACCELERATION LADDERS. EACH VARIANT IS A WHOLE 6-RUNG LADDER that plays as ONE continuous 36 s gesture, not a single texture to compare. Composer: \"at least one of the things I hope to use is this acceleration of speed and density... use the a version and then the b version and then the c version, and I might do that across models.\" So the ladder became the UNIT and the character became the swappable slot. Rungs: 6/9/12/15/18/22 attacks per s (rev 2s rungs, which the composer liked), 6 s each, gap 0. GAP 0 IS LOad-BEARING: the engine defaults spec.gap to 2, which would put 2 s of silence between every rung and destroy the accelerando. Each section emits its own timeline marker (engine :923), so the rungs are LABELLED when inserted. A-D hold one character across all six rungs; E changes character as it climbs; F is the same span as a SMOOTH bpm ramp (bpmEnd) instead of steps, so stepped-vs-continuous is one keypress. To reshape: name the rung and the character - e.g. \"make rung 3 gallop\" or \"rain ladder but stop at 15\". rev 1 (A/B/C refs), rev 2 (smear speed ladder), rev 3 (4x4 character x speed grid) all recoverable from git.",
